    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"The importance of having culture as part of their training is to equip them with the skills to be able to offer nursing care that is culturally competent, gender-sensitive and holistic\" says Samwel Gatimu, the supervising instructor who curated the Health and Culture week at the Aga Khan University School of Nursing and Midwifery (AKU-SONAM) in Kenya.",
